# The build context is the repo root (§14.1's `context: ../..`), and the COPY
# lines take whole directories — without this file they take the host's bin/
# and obj/ debris with them, and a Windows-restored obj/ inside a Linux build
# is a restore failure pointing at nothing. .git is excluded for size alone.
.git
**/bin
**/obj
TestResults

# .gitignore's "local configuration and secrets" section, mirrored: git
# ignoring a file does not keep it out of a build context, and a COPY of a
# whole source tree would carry a local appsettings into the published image.
**/appsettings.*.local.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
